{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2753 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "4b3370f435819847e0b78ffd84e523a6dd0cc6af2a1677b294f832af09d28929" :edb/db-before-t 2752 :edb/db-after-t 2753 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536065 50 #inst "2026-10-09T14:11:30.460Z" 13194139536065 true] [17592186059484 1100 "Calculate the minor of the entry $b_{21}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139536065 false] [17592186059484 1100 "Calculate the minor of the entry $b_{21}$ in the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/8e664813c6467d5bb06a8eb1e1d68778d3142479939624a7a46674f593d786b9.png)" 13194139536065 true] [17592186059484 1145 "The minor of $b_{21} = 3$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/a69955fcba387ef3c65f1c1529c2007d8d70f82d95738af9b995999a21198730.png)\n\nSo, the minor of $b_{21}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =2-35 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186059484 1145 "The minor of $b_{21} = 3$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of $b_{21}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =2-35 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536065 false] [17592186059485 1100 "What is the minor of $c_{22}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & 0 & -3y \\\\ 1 & x+2y & 4 \\\\ -y & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139536065 false] [17592186059485 1100 "What is the minor of $c_{22}$ in the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/1449dfd139653f75de7be2e27e86f0c9d2d8a5a17e25ae184b892f489ffbb71e.png)" 13194139536065 true] [17592186059485 1145 "First, we remove the second row and second column: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/09bd73c7e51abcad8efa354317519a2687601b3ccdbfea0ac2b6222f75b3397e.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7x\\cdot 5-(-3y)\\cdot (-y) \\\\  & =35x-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186059485 1145 "First, we remove the second row and second column: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & ∗ & -3y \\\\ ∗ & x+2y & ∗ \\\\ -y & ∗ & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7x\\cdot 5-(-3y)\\cdot (-y) \\\\  & =35x-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536065 false] [17592186059486 1100 "Given that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139536065 false] [17592186059486 1100 "Given that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/1d37ba9039f24a96be2d148c9f30c8a10ca30c9745ad8a28df23de5a42f6dcab.png)" 13194139536065 true] [17592186059486 1145 "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/80f9b95139f7b571c7752ee1feec4c9d3df8456223581736ae019344a6f9a080.png)\n\nThe minor of $a_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot 2k-3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+3 & =5 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =1 \\\\ k & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=1.$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186059486 1145 "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of $a_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot 2k-3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+3 & =5 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =1 \\\\ k & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=1.$" 13194139536065 false] [17592186059676 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381862 13194139536065 true] [17592186059676 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381890 13194139536065 true] [17592186059677 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381893 13194139536065 true] [17592186059677 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381899 13194139536065 true] [17592186059677 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381902 13194139536065 true] [17592186059677 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381906 13194139536065 true] [17592186059678 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381869 13194139536065 true] [17592186059678 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381876 13194139536065 true] [17592186059678 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381883 13194139536065 true] [17592186059678 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381896 13194139536065 true] [17592186059909 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536065 true] [17592186059909 1100 "Calculate the minor of the entry $y_{13}$ in the matrix\n\n$Y = \\begin{bmatrix}15 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139536065 false] [17592186059909 1100 "Calculate the minor of the entry ${y}_{13}$ in the matrix\n$Y=[\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186059909 1145 "The minor of ${y}_{13}=9$ (first row, third column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $9$ are removed: \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & 9 \\\\ 7 & 1 & ∗ \\\\ 0 & -1 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${y}_{13}=9$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-7-0 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186060063 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536065 true] [17592186060063 1100 "Given that the minor of $p_{23}$ is $t^{2} + 12$, find all the possible values of $t$ in the matrix\n\n$P = \\begin{bmatrix}t & -8 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139536065 false] [17592186060063 1100 "Given that the minor of ${p}_{23}$ is ${t}^{2}+12$, find all the possible values of $t$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}t & -8 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186060063 1145 "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}t & -8 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 4 \\\\ -1 & 9 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${p}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}t & -8 \\\\ -1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}t & -8 \\\\ -1 & 9\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t\\cdot 9-(-8)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =9t-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${p}_{23}$ is ${t}^{2}+12$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9t-8 & ={t}^{2}+12 \\\\ {t}^{2}-9t+20 & =0 \\\\ (t-5)(t-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $t=4$ and $t=5.$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381862 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381863 13194139536065 true] [17592186381862 1089 "q-1091" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381862 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536065 true] [17592186381862 1100 "Calculate the minor of the entry ${x}_{21}$ in the matrix\n$X=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 11\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381862 1113 #uuid "384e9c4f-c4b4-5e71-ae10-7eb74dbf658f" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381862 1145 "The minor of ${x}_{21}=-2$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${x}_{21}=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 11\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 11-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-33-0 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381864 13194139536065 true] [17592186381863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381865 13194139536065 true] [17592186381863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381866 13194139536065 true] [17592186381863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381867 13194139536065 true] [17592186381863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381868 13194139536065 true] [17592186381863 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536065 true] [17592186381863 1041 "selection" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381863 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381867 13194139536065 true] [17592186381863 1110 #uuid "059c44d3-1284-50ec-8ef0-7cbb4b697e49" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381864 1034 "26" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381864 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536065 true] [17592186381864 1111 #uuid "d57ec0fd-73b2-541b-aaee-acd985d2e80d" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381865 1034 "-8" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381865 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536065 true] [17592186381865 1111 #uuid "43bdc5a8-22ba-5f2e-a766-68682e19ca5a" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381866 1034 "82" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381866 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536065 true] [17592186381866 1111 #uuid "8968474e-b2c4-5336-b54f-d4492f49718d" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381867 1034 "-33" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381867 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536065 true] [17592186381867 1111 #uuid "75258219-ad34-596f-8f9b-bf0ecc86b17a" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381868 1034 "77" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381868 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536065 true] [17592186381868 1111 #uuid "7db46d9f-07ec-5b9c-aab2-0501c0dcff7a" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381869 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381870 13194139536065 true] [17592186381869 1089 "q-128082" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381869 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536065 true] [17592186381869 1100 "Given that the minor of ${p}_{11}$ is $4$, find all the possible values of $t$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-5t & 18 & 6t \\\\ -3 & 9 & 5 \\\\ 19t & 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381869 1113 #uuid "f60c5f2a-2917-5bd9-92a0-889883057b41" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381869 1145 "First, we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}5t & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 9 & 5 \\\\ ∗ & 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${p}_{11}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =9\\cdot 3t-5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =27t-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${p}_{11}$ is $4$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27t-5 & =4 \\\\ 27t & =9 \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t=\\frac{1}{3}.$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381871 13194139536065 true] [17592186381870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381872 13194139536065 true] [17592186381870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381873 13194139536065 true] [17592186381870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381874 13194139536065 true] [17592186381870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381875 13194139536065 true] [17592186381870 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536065 true] [17592186381870 1041 "selection" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381870 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381874 13194139536065 true] [17592186381870 1110 #uuid "6a6b4e57-94f1-5cd1-bb04-e4409b3403e1" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381871 1034 "t=23" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381871 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536065 true] [17592186381871 1111 #uuid "484161fc-5efa-5aac-a03c-cd6ab2ab4c53" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381872 1034 "t=\\frac{5}{6}" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381872 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536065 true] [17592186381872 1111 #uuid "fd9f2560-0558-5199-9f06-ef22d5c01a90" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381873 1034 "t=17" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381873 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536065 true] [17592186381873 1111 #uuid "a1af3526-161d-54dd-b94e-f9338ef39a6a" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381874 1034 "t=\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381874 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536065 true] [17592186381874 1111 #uuid "b74986d1-8b90-5461-899a-8f0c669bb5c8" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381875 1034 "t=\\frac{19}{3}" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536065 true] [17592186381875 1111 #uuid "2ba23472-c1c7-5ac7-aeb1-219a1500eed9" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381876 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381877 13194139536065 true] [17592186381876 1089 "q-18243" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381876 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536065 true] [17592186381876 1100 "Given that the minor of ${b}_{33}$ is $3$, find all the possible values of $x$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} & -10 \\\\ -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381876 1113 #uuid "279f1542-6c2c-5bb8-ac83-070b364b0b4a" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381876 1145 "First, we remove the third row and third column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} & ∗ \\\\ -5 & 8 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${b}_{33}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6\\cdot 8-(-5)\\cdot (-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =48-5{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${b}_{33}$ is $3$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}48-5{x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ 45-5{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 9-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (3-x)(3+x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-3$ and $x=3.$" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381878 13194139536065 true] [17592186381877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381879 13194139536065 true] [17592186381877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381880 13194139536065 true] [17592186381877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381881 13194139536065 true] [17592186381877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381882 13194139536065 true] [17592186381877 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536065 true] [17592186381877 1041 "selection" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381877 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381879 13194139536065 true] [17592186381877 1110 #uuid "aea8a39a-de0e-56d9-80ad-c3e3e4bc2a23" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381878 1034 "$x=6$ only" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536065 true] [17592186381878 1111 #uuid "9d671cbc-a741-5b99-908b-3f3bdb42c8ef" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381879 1034 "$x=-3$ and $x=3$ only" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536065 true] [17592186381879 1111 #uuid "979d73ec-6409-59f0-9fa2-6e16c2bdf06e" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381880 1034 "$x=9$ only" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536065 true] [17592186381880 1111 #uuid "7cf4a7f0-1295-53cf-9ded-45037759598a" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381881 1034 "$x=-9$ only" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381881 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536065 true] [17592186381881 1111 #uuid "bef5c8a2-98d6-573d-83b8-87bc45e7e052" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381882 1034 "$x=-9$ and $x=9$ only" 13194139536065 true] [17592186381882 1103 #edb/ref 175921